  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The symbol \\(|a|\\) means \\(a\\) if \\(a\\) is a positive number or zero, and \\(-a\\) if \\(a\\) is a negative number. For all real values of \\(t\\) the expression \\(\\sqrt{t^4+t^2}\\) is equal to:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(t^3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(t^2+t\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(|t^2+t|\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(t\\sqrt{t^2+1}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(|t|\\sqrt{1+t^2}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1961-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factoring inside the radical gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\sqrt{t^2(t^2+1)} &=\\sqrt{t^2}\\sqrt{t^2+1}\\\\ &=|t|\\sqrt{1+t^2}. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\(t^2\\) from under the radical",
        "For real \\(t,\\) \\(\\sqrt{t^2}=|t|\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
